[5.3963, "o", "\u001b[38;5;208m● belay\u001b[0m\r\n  Found your exports already sitting in the inbox — no need to drop anything. Two accounts, 24 months each (2024-07 to 2026-06):\r\n\r\n  | account | file pattern | mapping source |\r\n  |---|---|---|\r\n  | `main` | `main_*.csv` | matched a known bank preset exactly (semicolon CSV, decimal comma, `Y.m.d` dates) |\r\n  | `credit` | `credit_*.xlsx` | no known preset — sniffed by hand: sheet \"Transactions\", columns `Date`/`Amount`/`Merchant` |\r\n\r\n  Quick check before I write these in:\r\n\r\n  1. Name/type OK? — `main` as a **checking** account, `credit` as a **credit_card**, both EUR?\r\n  2. For `credit`, the `Merchant` column doubles as the description (no separate counterparty column) — that fine, or does your card export usually have more detail than this sample shows?\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36malex ▸ \u001b[0m"]
