[26.6432, "o", "  Your files cover exactly what the filenames suggest: 24 months, **2024-07 to 2026-06**, no gaps.\r\n\r\n  **Income:** \"EMPLOYER\" pays **€2,800 on the 1st of every month, all 24/24 months** — no missed or doubled months, so this really is steady, not just clustered.\r\n\r\n  Here's what else the data shows, with proposed categories:\r\n\r\n  | Description | Pattern | Amount | Proposed category |\r\n  |---|---|---|---|\r\n  | STREAMFLIX | day 5, every month | ~€12.22 | Subscriptions |\r\n  | CLOUDTUNES | day 6, every month | ~€12.54 | Subscriptions |\r\n  | FUEL STATION A1 | day 14, every month | ~€75.65 | Transport |\r\n  | GREEN MARKET | 54× over 24mo | ~€77.87 avg | Groceries |\r\n  | DEMO SUPERMARKET 12 | 42× over 24mo | ~€83.26 avg | Groceries |\r\n  | PIZZA PRONTO | 27× over 24mo | ~€26.29 avg | Dining out |\r\n  | SUSHI GO | 14× over 24mo | ~€26.42 avg | Dining out |\r\n\r\n  Two checks:\r\n  1. Categories/groupings look right, or want to rename/split any (e.g. keep Green Market and Demo Supermarket both as \"Groceries,\" or separate)?\r\n  2. Salary goes under a category called \"Salary\" — good, or do you call it something else?\r\n\r\n"]
[26.6433, "o", "\u001b[1;36malex ▸ \u001b[0m"]
